# SESSION RESUME — read NEXT.md first

`NEXT.md` (repo root) is the working roadmap / decision pad for this OB1 Life Engine
checkout. It is **gitignored** (local only — never commit it).

When the user says **`next`**, **`dccpr`**, or resumes mid-stream:

1. Read `NEXT.md` before acting.
2. Summarize current state in a few lines.
3. Surface open **Decisions needed** and wait for John to pick — do not start a
   feature wave until a priority/branch decision is clear.
4. Refresh live facts (branch, `git status`, watchdog/socket, open PR) if the
   file looks stale, then update `NEXT.md`.

If `NEXT.md` is missing, rebuild it from `PROJECT.md`, `STATUS.md`, `BACKLOG.md`,
`git status` / `git log origin/main..HEAD`, and runtime checks (`ob1-watchdog`,
`/tmp/ob1.sock`, `sbbrain`).
